{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_106","type":"agent_message","text":"The SIGFPE is C’s actual behavior for zero-width simplified writes, so that generic boundary cannot be exercised in-process. I’m moving potentially fatal simplified API cases into isolated child invocations of the same test binary, one library at a time. The parent will compare exact returned state for normal rejections and exact termination status for fatal boundaries, while keeping nonfatal sentinels in-process."}}
